g drawn as mounted: HDMI end UP, USB-C down -> J5 = left row (ESP side), J6 = right row (ADC side).\n2. AD9226: module P2 header faces J6, +5V row at the top. All 14 signals sit on J6-14..J6-1 in the header's\n   own top-to-bottom order (D0..D6, CLK, OTR, D7..D11) -> short, nearly straight wires. CLK (J6-7) and OTR\n   (J6-6) are on the LED1/LED0 pins (LED0 is lit while OTR=0, normal). Data pins have no LED/pull-up load\n   except D3 (HDMI HPD 2.2k+5.1k divider) and D8 (microSD 10k pull-up) - both light.\n   P2 pin order was read from the seller photo - VERIFY on the real board. Bit order: BIT_REVERSE parameter.\n3. AD9226 power: +5V/GND from Tang J5-1/J5-2 for bring-up (wire under the Tang); a separate clean 5V is\n   better for the SDR. Its logic outputs are 3.3V - measure the module's 3V3 pad before connecting data.\n4. TFT: RESET/DC/MOSI/SCK from J6-18..J6-15 (LED3/4/5/2 pins - they flicker), CS from J5-18,\n   VCC from J6-19, GND from J6-20, LED (backlight) -> 3V3. SDO and touch pins unconnected.\n5. Pins NOT used on purpose: 76/86 (driven by onboard BL616), 49 (LCD backlight boost EN),\n   54/55/56/51 (onboard audio amp - reserved for SDR audio).\n6. ESP32-S3 link (2026-11-08), straight jumpers J5-n <-> ESP J3-(23-n): SCK 53/GPIO1, MISO 71/GPIO2\n   (phase 3, J5-18 is TFT CS until the TFT moves to the ESP), I2S WS 72/GPIO42, MOSI 79/GPIO39 (WS2812 DIN),\n   I2S BCK 41/GPIO47, I2S DATA 42/GPIO21, CS_N 80/GPIO20, GND J5-2/J3-21. See hardware/system.\n7. microSD slot must stay EMPTY (ADC_D8 and ESP_I2S_BCK use SD D1/D2 lines)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 200.66 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "197772cf-6e41-5c3b-a351-b35507779f78")) (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1"))))
